# init.recovery.usb.rc
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (do not delete)
# -----------------------------------
# TWRP-11's system/etc/init/hw/init.rc contains:
#     import /init.recovery.usb.rc
# and AOSP init's parser treats an unreadable `import` as a FATAL error and
# calls init.abort(). The result is: init aborts -> kernel panic
# ("Attempted to kill init!") -> bootloader watchdog resets after ~8 s ->
# endless reboot loop / fastboot.
#
# WHY THE BODY IS EMPTY
# ---------------------
# BoardConfig.mk sets TW_EXCLUDE_DEFAULT_USB_INIT := true, which means TWRP
# deliberately does NOT ship its own USB config for this device. Putting an
# AOSP adbd recipe here would fight TWRP's own USB handling (TWRP configures
# the gadget from userspace via android.hardware.usb.gadget).
#
# So: satisfy the import with an empty file. An empty .rc is valid and adds
# zero behaviour.
#
# If you later WANT TWRP's own USB init, flip
#     TW_EXCLUDE_DEFAULT_USB_INIT := false
# in BoardConfig.mk, delete this file, and let TWRP's copy through instead.
